       "v": "INPUTS / LOGIC / LIMITS — Inputs: current backlog (linked live from this workbook's dashboard), daily intake, analyst count, cases per analyst per day, complex-case share, and a complex-case handling multiplier. Logic: effective capacity = analysts x cases/day, divided by the blended handling factor ((1 - complex share) + complex share x multiplier); net cleared = capacity - intake; days to clear = backlog / net, rounded up; the projection subtracts net per day and floors at zero. Limits: a simple linear planning model — it assumes intake and capacity stay constant and treats complexity only through the share x multiplier assumption, both of which the visitor sets. It plans staffing; it does not measure the live queue."
